    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> (1897) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> (1916) ruled through the Tutsi king and treated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> and Tutsi as different races; Belgium's identity cards of 1935 fixed the labels, and the Hutu revolution of 1959 drove over 100,000 Tutsi into exile before independence on 1 July 1962.</li><li>Between 500,000 and 1,000,000 Tutsi and moderate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> were killed in about 100 days from 6 April 1994 in attacks planned and ordered by the interim government; the RPF's military victory in July ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>.</li><li>Under the RPF and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-kagame">Paul Kagame</a>, president since 2000, poverty fell from 60.3% in 2000 to 27.4% in 2024 and the economy grew 9.4% in 2025, while elections are manipulated and Human Rights Watch documents detention, disappearances and torture.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Rwanda joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-nations">Commonwealth of Nations</a> in 2009 as one of its few members with no historical link to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>, and in 2008 it changed the medium of instruction in its schools from French to English.</p></aside>
    </section>

