oire-kayibanda">Grégoire Kayibanda</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1973</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juvenal-habyarimana">Juvénal Habyarimana</a> takes power in a military coup; pro-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> discrimination continues with less violence and more prosperity.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1990</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rwandan-patriotic-front">Rwandan Patriotic Front</a>, formed of Tutsi refugees, invades northern Rwanda from Uganda, beginning the Rwandan Civil War.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1994</span><span class="rf-text">On 6 April Habyarimana's plane is shot down near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kigali">Kigali</a>; within hours the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> begins, killing 500,000 to 1,000,000 Tutsi and moderate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> in about 100 days.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">July 1994</span><span class="rf-text">The RPF takes control of the whole country, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>; some two million <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> flee to Zaïre and other neighbours.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2000</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-kagame">Paul Kagame</a>, the RPF's former commander, becomes president; a constitution follows in 2003 after a national referendum.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2025</span><span class="rf-text">On 25 January the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a> severs diplomatic relations over Rwanda's support for the M23 rebellion after the Goma offensive.</span></li></ol>
